Phase 18 remoting code-description locale parity and current local gate —
2026-10-22 17:12 UTC

Code revision: `a4136667`. Branch: `phase/18-phase-18-compatibility-closure`.
Environment: macOS AArch64, Apple M5 Max, 18 logical CPUs, Rust 1.85.0.
Pinned Java reference: RocketMQ client 5.5.1, commit
`efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`.

Compatibility slice:
- Pinned `RemotingHelper` initializes public request/response code maps by
  applying no-argument `String.toLowerCase()` to Java field names. Rust code
  descriptions now use a one-time locale snapshot from `LC_ALL`, `LC_CTYPE`,
  then `LANG`, and produce the Turkish/Azeri dotless `ı` mapping for ASCII `I`.
- The Java fixture sets `Locale` to `tr-TR`, compares all 166 request and 68
  response code descriptions and unknown-code fallbacks, and restores the
  original locale in `finally`. Fixture SHA-256:
  `f6f8ebff1b2cfb33bd7234d8268b5747583f18f98f57fa4017d2af4f204a2573`.
- One Maven run exposed that the fixture needed to restore global JVM locale:
  typed-header scenario IDs were generated with Turkish uppercase. The fixture
  now restores locale on success and failure. A full offline Maven verify
  passes and leaves all unrelated typed-header fixtures clean.

